+### When the code is gone rather than different
+
+A distribution that changed is refused with `extension_version_mismatch`. A
+workflow that is no longer served **at all** — `ext remove`, a deleted directory,
+a package that failed to load — is a different stop: the task parks with
+`workflow_missing: <workflow>`, from the open-time guard, from a hot reload, or
+from the scheduler on the next scan.
+
+What the two have in common is that the record survives the code. The
+distribution the task is pinned to stays in the project's runtime index and stays
+undeletable while an open task names it, so the one statement of what that task
+needs is not dropped at the moment the code behind it disappears.
+
